Recently I killed a cockatrice, but was without gloves.  This question
then came to mind: What if you could grease your hands?  (Currently
getting your fingers greasy does not protect them, from cockatrices at
least.)

My proposal is for a bottle of Vaseline.  You would (a)pply it to give
your hands a good coating.  They would then become slippery for maybe
a couple hundred turns or until you used a towel.  However, during
that time, they would be protected from such things as cockatrices
and... at the moment, I can't think of anything else.

I suppose some other provisions would have to be made to make this
YANI more than a one-trick horse; oh well.

On a side note, Vaseline could also give you nicer hands for a while,
although the moisturizing effect wouldn't have much practical
application outside of that--AFAIK no skin-chapping-related maladies
have been implemented yet.

